5
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:08,820
Okay.

6
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:17,480
Back on?

7
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:19,060
This is fun.

8
00:01:19,060 --> 00:01:19,860
We could do this for a while.

9
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:26,300
I read online that if the pastor sees a shadow this morning, it'll be Groundhog Day.

10
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:27,680
There'll be six more weeks of this series.

11
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,160
Is that right?

12
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:31,320
All right.

13
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:37,560
I'm going to read you guys a story this morning of story time.

14
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:42,100
And it's a story that we have covered before.

15
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:47,400
Michelle talked about it several weeks ago, and Ryan read it when we started this series,

16
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,020
so it seems fitting to revisit it today.

17
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:53,340
It's the story of Paul and Silas, right?

18
00:01:54,500 --> 00:02:01,160
In Acts 16, Paul and Silas, they've gone to the city of Philippi in Macedonia on a modern map

19
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,720
that's in the eastern arm of Greece.

20
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:05,480
And they found a community there.

21
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:07,600
They've begun to pray with this community.

22
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,060
They've baptized a few folks.

23
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:12,380
They've shared the gospel of Christ.

24
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:16,240
And then Luke, who's with them, records this story for us about what happens.

25
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:19,680
And we'll pick it up in verse 16, where Luke says,

26
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:25,040
As we were going to the place of prayer, we were met by a slave girl who had a spirit of divination

27
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:28,440
that brought her owners much gain by fortune-telling.

28
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:30,520
I should...

29
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:34,420
Is it not in there?

30
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:35,420
I'll just read it to you.

31
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:35,800
Okay.

32
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:38,260
My apologies.

33
00:02:38,260 --> 00:02:40,500
Much gain by fortune-telling.

34
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:45,020
She followed Paul and Silas, crying out,

35
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:49,740
These men are servants of the Most High God who proclaim to you the way of salvation.

36
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:51,940
And she kept doing this for many days.

37
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:56,200
And Paul, having become greatly annoyed, turned and said to the spirit,

38
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:59,060
I command you, in the name of Jesus Christ, come out of her.

39
00:02:59,060 --> 00:03:00,400
And it came out that very hour.

40
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:03,440
But when her owners saw that their hope of gain was gone,

41
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:07,440
they seized Paul and Silas and dragged them into the marketplace before the rulers.

42
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:10,380
And when they brought them to the magistrates, they said,

43
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:12,820
These men are Jews, and they're disturbing our city.

44
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:17,280
They advocate customs that are not lawful for us as Romans to accept or practice.

45
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,860
Made it a racial thing, right?

46
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:20,200
They're not like one of us.

47
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:23,320
The crowd joined in attacking them.

48
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:28,360
And the magistrates tore off their garments and gave orders to beat them with rods.

49
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:32,280
And when they'd inflicted many blows upon them, they threw them into prison,

50
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:34,500
ordering the jailer to keep them safely.

51
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:36,760
And having received this order, he put them in the inner prison,

52
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:38,160
and he fastened their feet in stocks.

53
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:42,800
And about midnight, Paul and Silas were praying and singing hymns to God.

54
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:45,200
And the prisoners were listening to them.

55
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:47,040
And suddenly there was a great earthquake.

56
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:49,440
So the foundations of the prison were shaken.

57
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:53,060
And immediately all the doors were opened and everyone's bonds were unfastened.

58
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,600
When the jailer woke and saw that the prison doors were open,

59
00:03:55,600 --> 00:04:00,280
he drew his sword and was about to kill himself, supposing that his prisoners had escaped.

60
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:02,920
But Paul cried out with a loud voice,

61
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:04,520
Don't harm yourself, we're all here.

62
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:07,800
And the jailer called for lights and rushed in and trembling with fear,

63
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,840
he fell down before Paul and Silas.

64
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:11,860
And then he brought them out and said,

65
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:13,460
Sirs, what must I do to be saved?

66
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:14,260
And they said,

67
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:17,640
Believe in the Lord Jesus and you will be saved, you and your household.

68
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:21,560
And they spoke the word of the Lord to him, to all who were with him in his house.

69
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:25,840
And he took them that same hour of the night into his house, washed their wounds.

70
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:28,780
And he was baptized at once, he and all his family.

71
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:30,900
He brought them up into his house and set food before them.

72
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:34,580
And he rejoiced along with his entire household that he had believed in God.

73
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:35,780
Word of the Lord.

74
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:45,820
So, there are elements in that story that underline why our church,

75
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:48,800
Canvas Community Church, has the mission and vision that we do.

76
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:49,220
Okay?

77
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:54,640
And we're going to, it records Paul and Silas boldly and joyfully leading people

78
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:56,800
to reconciliation in God, right?

79
00:04:56,880 --> 00:05:01,120
Like the prodigal son coming back to the father, turning around, changing his ways, coming back.

80
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:06,920
And in the midst, they're doing this in the midst of what could have been a tragic story of injustice and pain.

81
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:10,200
But somehow it wasn't in that story, which is unusual.

82
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:13,420
So, let's review our vision and mission here.

83
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:16,300
And we'll see how they map to that story.

84
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:16,520
Okay?

85
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:23,980
First of all, every church, Ryan says this all the time, every church has the same mission, right?

86
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:25,200
It's the Great Commission.

87
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:27,020
It's from Matthew 18.

88
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:28,900
It's repeated, excuse me, Matthew 28.

89
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:32,680
It's repeated in Luke 24 and in short form in Mark.

90
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:34,480
And it's repeated in Acts 1.

91
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:35,540
He tells us what?

92
00:05:35,580 --> 00:05:40,540
To go into all the world, share the gospel, make disciples, baptize people into his name.

93
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:42,300
That's the mission of the church.

94
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:45,320
Bring people, reconcile them back to Christ.

95
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:47,040
Bring them back to God.

96
00:05:48,020 --> 00:05:53,980
But the implementation of this mission looks very different depending on your access to

97
00:05:53,980 --> 00:06:00,160
communication technology, your cultural habits, the makeup of your community, your skills,

98
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:02,640
your affluence sometimes, who you're near.

99
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:07,600
All these things can really change how you go about it, specifically how it looks.

100
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,720
So, what we do, of course, is we verbalize our mission.

101
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:12,700
We say, given what we have, how are we going to do this Great Commission?

102
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:14,120
What are the steps we're going to take?

103
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:16,780
And so, we verbalize it, we write it down, and that's our mission and our vision.

104
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:20,080
To get us all pointed in the same direction.

105
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:26,060
So, our vision is cultivating God's kingdom on earth by proclaiming Jesus clearly and obeying

106
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:27,380
Jesus boldly.

107
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:29,400
Now, that's what we want to see happen, right?

108
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:30,580
That's the picture.

109
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:33,240
When things work right, that's what it's going to look like.

110
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:42,060
We're going to be cultivating God's kingdom on earth by proclaiming Jesus clearly and obeying

111
00:06:42,060 --> 00:06:42,800
Jesus boldly.

112
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:46,060
Our mission is what we're going to do to make that happen, right?

113
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:53,500
So, as Ryan has said, the mission, inviting real people with real lives into a Christ-centered

114
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:55,380
community, is supposed to make that picture happen.

115
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:59,640
And if you don't see how that can lead to that, you're in the right place, because that's what

116
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:00,160
we're going to talk about.

117
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:00,740
Okay?

118
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:01,980
Okay?

119
00:07:01,980 --> 00:07:03,240
Good.

120
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:07,780
So, our vision says, when we get it right, that's what it's going to look like.

121
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:11,480
Our mission says, we're going to be a church that invites real people into real lives,

122
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:15,660
into a Christian community, real people with real lives, which is to say, we're going to

123
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:17,760
bring people in to send them out, right?

124
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:19,660
We're bringing you in to send you out.

125
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:21,480
This is what Michelle talked about last week.

126
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:26,160
We bring folks into a Christ-centered community where they are soaked in the gospel and in

127
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:27,160
Scripture and in prayer.

128
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:29,580
And the gospel is transformational.

129
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:31,460
Transforms lives.

130
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:36,800
And people are then going out with transformed lives, as she said, with prophets, priests,

131
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:37,820
and ambassadors, notably.

132
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:39,420
We're going to talk about ambassadors today.

133
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:43,800
And this is how Paul saw it working.

134
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,740
Paul saw the church working this way.

135
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:50,220
And we know that because about five years after the story that we read today, he wrote

136
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:56,780
a letter to the church in Corinth after he'd been miraculously freed from prison here in

137
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:59,720
Philippi, explaining what sounds a little bit like a mission statement.

138
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:04,560
But it was at least a clear description of what they should be doing with themselves.

139
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:07,740
And I'm sorry, that's the wrong button.

140
00:08:07,740 --> 00:08:08,460
They should.

141
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:15,040
So in 2 Corinthians 5, 17 to 20, he says, therefore, if anyone is in Christ, he's a new creation,

142
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:15,720
right?

143
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:16,940
That's what Michelle talked about.

144
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:18,480
Transformation power of the gospel.

145
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:21,520
You've become a new creation from having joined in Christ.

146
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:22,580
The old has passed away.

147
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:24,040
Behold, the new has come.

148
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:29,620
And all this is from God, who through Christ reconciled us to himself and gave us the ministry

149
00:08:29,620 --> 00:08:30,400
of reconciliation.

150
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:34,260
He reconciled us to himself and gave us the ministry of reconciliation.

151
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:39,940
That is, in Christ, God was reconciling the world to himself, not counting the trespasses

152
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:43,040
against him, and entrusting to us that message of reconciliation.

153
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:48,500
Therefore, we are ambassadors for Christ, making his appeal through us.

154
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:52,560
We implore you, on behalf of Christ, be reconciled to God, right?

155
00:08:52,560 --> 00:09:02,940
So we are cultivating—should we understand, then, that our church is an ambassador academy?

156
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:04,960
Is that what we are?

157
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:07,120
I mean, it sort of is, right?

158
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:11,260
Except that we don't have classes, we don't have requirements, we don't have fees, we don't

159
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:15,200
have—there's not a set of things you have to do to graduate, right?

160
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:19,920
What we're doing is cultivating a relationship here with the divine, which is going to lead

161
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:23,220
you to a lifestyle that's going to produce the fruit, all right?

162
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:24,700
That's how it's supposed to work.

163
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:25,960
And this was Christ's approach.

164
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:30,740
We know that because we see in the Gospels that he walked with his disciples daily for

165
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:31,260
years.

166
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:33,000
He walked with them all the way.

167
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,040
He let them walk with him.

168
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,780
They got to know each other over the course of years.

169
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:38,020
They became to know the mystery that was Christ.

170
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:43,820
And then, in Matthew 10, Mark 6, Luke 9, the Gospels record that he put them in pairs

171
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:49,320
of two and sent them out on a trial run to go see what it was like to spread the Gospel.

172
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:52,200
And what they found was that their relationship with the world had been changed.

173
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:55,240
They had been transformed by the Gospel and went out to spread it.

174
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:59,880
They had a different view of their relationship to mankind, and they were inviting them to

175
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:00,600
be reconciled.

176
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:04,920
So in some circles, there's this running debate.

177
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:06,880
Is the church a hospital?

178
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:10,280
Is this a place where you come to heal the wounded and brokenhearted?

179
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:13,860
Is this a school where you come to learn about God or morality?

180
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:16,300
Is this an outpost in the struggle against sin and evil?

181
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:19,680
Is this a worship center where we come to encounter the worship and divine?

182
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:21,480
Encounter the divine and worship him?

183
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:25,700
Our mission and vision statement says, yes, all those are true, right?

184
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:26,800
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

185
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:27,620
This is a hospital.

186
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:33,860
Our church serves all those functions in the service of bringing folks in, healing them

187
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:39,460
up, helping them grow in relationship with Christ, to get them equipped to go out and

188
00:10:39,460 --> 00:10:41,800
speak clearly and obey boldly.

189
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:47,080
In fact, we're equipping them to be ambassadors of Christ, boldly and joyfully spreading the

190
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:48,340
Gospel that leads to reconciliation.

191
00:10:48,340 --> 00:10:51,000
That's what the church is for.

192
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,280
That's what our mission and vision says.

193
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:58,820
So, cultivating God's kingdom is preparing the soil, right?

194
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:00,660
It's a farming term.

195
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:02,060
We're putting down seeds.

196
00:11:02,060 --> 00:11:03,020
We're smoothing out the soil.

197
00:11:03,020 --> 00:11:03,920
We're getting rid of weeds.

198
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:04,740
We're cultivating.

199
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:05,820
We're not building something.

200
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:06,580
There's no blueprint.

201
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:10,800
We're not going to have something done in six months or a year or ten years.

202
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:12,900
We're cultivating the soil so God can grow it.

203
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:15,980
And what are we growing?

204
00:11:15,980 --> 00:11:17,960
God's kingdom, not ours.

205
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:21,680
When we talk frequently about not wanting to plant a new church and not wanting to build

206
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:24,020
a bigger building, it's kind of a reflection of the fact that we're not going to

207
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:27,420
that we want the kingdom of God to grow and we're not trying to build anything ourselves.

208
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:30,140
It's not the walls that matter, right?

209
00:11:30,140 --> 00:11:32,940
And where are we building that?

210
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:34,240
Where are we cultivating this to grow?

211
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:35,300
We're on earth.

212
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:39,260
The implication of that is here, now, not somewhere else later.

213
00:11:39,260 --> 00:11:39,860
Now.

214
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:44,360
Are we going to see the kingdom of God in its full fruition in our lifetime?

215
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,380
Probably not.

216
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:47,560
All Christians have wanted that.

217
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:48,500
I'd love it if it happened.

218
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:52,560
What we are going to see is growth and God working in the lives of the people that we

219
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:53,200
reach out to.

220
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:58,520
And the people that we invite in to our Christian community so that they then go out and speak

221
00:11:58,520 --> 00:12:01,980
boldly and obey boldly, speak clearly and obey boldly.

222
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:05,360
So it's now, here, not Jesus.

223
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,520
And what are we proclaiming?

224
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:08,980
We're proclaiming Jesus, clearly.

225
00:12:08,980 --> 00:12:11,420
Not a Jesus adjacent agenda.

226
00:12:11,420 --> 00:12:12,180
Right?

227
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:14,660
This isn't a service.

228
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:19,360
It isn't a method of systematic morality that we're trying to pull you into or something

229
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:20,180
we're trying to get you to do.

230
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:23,380
We're just proclaiming Jesus boldly because he's going to bring the increase.

231
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:26,580
And we're obeying Jesus boldly.

232
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:27,940
Let's talk about boldly for a minute.

233
00:12:27,940 --> 00:12:36,200
Paul, in the story, went to this new city, Philippi, and he proclaimed the gospel to folks

234
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:37,220
who had never heard of it.

235
00:12:37,220 --> 00:12:38,720
I didn't really want to hear about it at first.

236
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:41,260
And he was there to stay indefinitely.

237
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:44,840
He was just going to stay until the job was done or God moved him on.

238
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:48,120
That is kind of bold, if you can imagine doing that.

239
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:57,420
In verse 18, he commands, with apparent expectation that it would happen, a spirit of divination

240
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:59,320
to leave this poor slave girl that it was torturing.

241
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:06,480
And that took her away from the people that were using her.

242
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:13,020
So in his annoyance, he reaches out with the love of Jesus to take this poor girl out of

243
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:13,460
her troubles.

244
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:15,840
Boldly, in front of everybody.

245
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,380
What if it hadn't worked?

246
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:19,320
That would be embarrassing.

