00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:54,140
Because he knows, he spit years in the details of cartography.

302
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:58,440
The things I think about that I know about well are the things that I've done over and over.

303
00:15:58,440 --> 00:15:59,060
I've touched it.

304
00:15:59,060 --> 00:15:59,720
I've felt it.

305
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:01,700
I know it inside and out.

306
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:04,560
And when you contradict me, I'm not likely to fight about it.

307
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:07,540
I'm just likely to wait until you actually have a real question and then I'll tell you about it.

308
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:08,280
All right?

309
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:11,340
If you want to know about golf, ask Ryan.

310
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:16,400
It's the thing you spend lots and lots of time with, right?

311
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:19,980
So boldness comes from confidence.

312
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,200
Confidence comes from certainty.

313
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,780
Certainty comes from familiarity.

314
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:26,140
Familiarity comes from time spent with it.

315
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:29,420
That's where the boldness comes from.

316
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:34,380
The secret to acting boldly is not willfulness.

317
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:35,340
It's not moxie.

318
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:36,200
It's not assertiveness.

319
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,540
It's not getting yourself worked up.

320
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:41,920
When I look back on my moments of significant boldness in my life and things I can't believe I did,

321
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:44,500
I was never trying to be bold.

322
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:49,500
I was acting out of immediate focused certainty that what I was doing was right.

323
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:55,400
And how do we develop that folks' certainty in Christ?

324
00:16:55,400 --> 00:17:01,160
We spend time seeking his voice in Christian community and Scripture and in prayer,

325
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:06,060
which is why we bring you into real lives to Christ-centered community.

326
00:17:06,060 --> 00:17:06,920
That's the point.

327
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:08,620
That's our mission statement.

328
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:11,840
We bring real people with real lives into Christ-centered community.

329
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:17,280
That's, I don't know where it is.

330
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:17,520
Okay.

331
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:20,700
You'll have to imagine it.

332
00:17:20,700 --> 00:17:25,280
Real people with real lives into Christ-centered community

333
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:30,800
so that we can then send them out as ambassadors to Christ,

334
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:33,060
cultivating God's kingdom on earth,

335
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:36,720
contributing to the growth of a thing that's here and now that's his, not ours,

336
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:39,840
by proclaiming it clearly and obeying it boldly.

337
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:40,780
There we go.

338
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:41,100
Thank you.

339
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:44,340
Now we need to get to the vision.

340
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:48,740
So we talked about boldly.

341
00:17:48,740 --> 00:17:50,600
What about proclaiming clearly?

342
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:52,220
What is it that Paul's proclaiming clearly?

343
00:17:52,220 --> 00:17:56,920
Sorry, I don't know where I am in the slides here.

344
00:17:56,920 --> 00:18:00,000
We've gone to the end somehow.

345
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:03,360
But what is it Paul's proclaiming clearly?

346
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:05,480
It's in this passage five times.

347
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:09,380
It says, he says, it's reconciliation, right?

348
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:10,460
That's what he's proclaiming.

349
00:18:10,620 --> 00:18:12,160
Like the story of the prodigal son.

350
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:16,000
The father is waiting with open arms if you just turn around, right?

351
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:20,760
Repent, for those who don't know, means to turn.

352
00:18:20,760 --> 00:18:23,320
You're walking one direction, turn and change directions.

353
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:24,580
That's what repent means.

354
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:28,200
You're going here, you realize it's the wrong way, you turn around and go this way.

355
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:33,420
In terms of reconciliation, reconciliation is etymologically to break something that's broken.

356
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:39,020
Definitionally, the way we use it, it's to heal a relationship, two people that have had a rift.

357
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:41,360
Two groups that can no longer communicate.

358
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:42,800
You want to reconcile them together.

359
00:18:42,800 --> 00:18:48,580
Christ, the gospel of reconciliation is you're resisting God.

360
00:18:48,580 --> 00:18:50,280
You're moving away from God.

361
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:53,300
You think he's fighting you because you're fighting him, right?

362
00:18:53,980 --> 00:18:56,480
Someone tells you there's a gospel, you should repent, you should turn.

363
00:18:56,480 --> 00:18:57,660
Go back to God.

364
00:18:57,660 --> 00:19:01,340
And when you do, you see he's standing there with open arms wanting to welcome you.

365
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:02,760
In the story of the prodigal son.

366
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:04,000
C.S. Lewis.

367
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:12,360
So, yeah, so step one then is making, step one of making our vision a reality is engendering boldness by immersion,

368
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:17,380
immersing ourselves in prayer, Scripture, and Christian community, which deepens daily our relationship with God.

369
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:22,060
And step two, knowing how to proclaim, that really comes out of the same thing, right?

370
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:29,840
Paul and Silas did, when they were reconciled with God, see that they were endowed with a ministry of reconciling others.

371
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:34,700
That's why, in that moment of stress, they were most focused on and most excited about the jailer hearing the gospel.

372
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:36,480
Because that was their focus.

373
00:19:38,320 --> 00:19:44,240
And we see that that was more important to Paul and Silas than their justice, they definitely had been treated unjustly,

374
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:47,360
than their freedom, they didn't try to get away, or their safety even.

375
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:53,540
They weren't focused on any of those things, they were focused on his eternal safety, reconciliation with God.

376
00:19:53,540 --> 00:20:05,020
And, as a parenthetical note, that led Paul and Silas to build a church which became their primary backers through the rest of Paul's ministry.

377
00:20:05,020 --> 00:20:07,120
They really stood by him when everything was going down.

378
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:13,120
And this was the bedrock that he, church, that he really first got his ministry on solid feet.

379
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:16,400
So, C.S. Lewis says it this way.

380
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:25,340
In Mere Christianity, which, by the way, I've said before, top five books that every Christian should read.

381
00:20:25,340 --> 00:20:26,340
This is the top of my list.

382
00:20:26,340 --> 00:20:28,780
If you haven't read it, please go buy it and read it, Mere Christianity.

383
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:30,400
He says in there,

384
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:33,300
Fallen man is not simply an imperfect creature who needs improvement.

385
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:34,540
We haven't just sinned.

386
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:36,780
He's a rebel who must lay down his arms.

387
00:20:36,780 --> 00:20:38,340
We've sinned and we're resisting God.

388
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:46,120
So, the people out there who are resisting this God, whose image they bear, it seems insane to them to say,

389
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:48,340
Just repent, turn around, go back to the guy you're fighting.

390
00:20:48,340 --> 00:20:49,120
Right?

391
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:56,580
That's why you need the ambassadors to go out on his behalf and say, please be reconciled.

392
00:20:56,580 --> 00:20:57,240
Please repent.

393
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:59,040
To explain this to them.

394
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:02,480
And when I say them, it was all of us, presumably.

395
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:02,980
Right?

396
00:21:04,420 --> 00:21:06,140
We're rebels that must lay down our arms.

397
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:16,380
When we're actively running and struggling, we can't tell what the right direction is, but like the father and the prodigal son, we see him there with arms open, wanting to welcome back the one who bears his image, his son.

398
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:17,580
That's us.

399
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:21,100
Now, some of you may be skeptical about that.

400
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:23,420
And some of the people you talk to may be skeptical about that.

401
00:21:23,420 --> 00:21:30,460
That claim that church seeks reconciliation and relationship because they have experience and because they've read the Bible.

402
00:21:30,460 --> 00:21:30,860
Right?

403
00:21:31,380 --> 00:21:37,780
And in their experience, a church is full of rules and they've read the Bible and it has, what, the Ten Commandments?

404
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:43,900
At first blush, without thinking it through, that does not sound like a list of how to reconcile, although I would argue that it is.

405
00:21:43,900 --> 00:21:45,260
But it doesn't sound that way.

406
00:21:45,260 --> 00:21:45,980
Right?

407
00:21:45,980 --> 00:21:56,640
They've attended unending Sunday school classes, maybe as children, where they were told to be kind, love one another, all these really good things, but they're a list of rules, things you're supposed to do.

408
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:57,920
How's that a relationship, they say.

409
00:21:59,280 --> 00:22:06,460
In many of the New Testament letters, 1 Peter 3 and 4 is two complete chapters of just a list of how you should behave.

410
00:22:06,460 --> 00:22:06,760
Right?

411
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:08,520
And you've read that.

412
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:15,920
So you say, how is this, is this, is this really a mystical relationship you're asking me into or is this an ethical requirement?

413
00:22:15,920 --> 00:22:18,380
Is this a series of ethical worldview?

414
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:19,480
Is it a behavioral list?

415
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:25,320
And to answer that, I would like to refer you all to the expectations that we place on marriage.

416
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:25,960
Okay?

417
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:32,320
There are a set of ethical behaviors we expect from our spouse, kindness, faithfulness, reliability, others.

418
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:40,020
And surely, these are expressions of, evidence of, love and devotion.

419
00:22:40,020 --> 00:22:40,840
Right?

420
00:22:40,840 --> 00:22:45,720
They're not because marriage vows present us with a list of onerous responsibilities.

421
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:48,540
Faithfulness is evidence of love, we think.

422
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:51,940
It also sounds, it's also grounds for more confidence in that love.

423
00:22:51,940 --> 00:23:03,560
So I would just like you to raise your hand publicly if you think it's reasonable to ask your spouse, is this a relationship or a list of ethical responsibilities?

424
00:23:08,860 --> 00:23:09,220
No.

425
00:23:09,220 --> 00:23:09,740
Okay.

426
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:10,580
No takers.

427
00:23:10,580 --> 00:23:17,280
Because we know the behavior is an outflow of the evidence of the committed relationship.

428
00:23:17,280 --> 00:23:17,640
Right?

429
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:22,300
We hear what God says and we act on it as part of understanding him.

430
00:23:22,300 --> 00:23:25,520
That's what the Hebrew word shema is, to hear and obey.

431
00:23:25,520 --> 00:23:26,360
To hear is to obey.

432
00:23:26,360 --> 00:23:31,900
Christ explains that to his New Testament audience with the parable of the house on the solid ground versus sand.

433
00:23:32,440 --> 00:23:35,600
You hear my words, you do them, it's like building your house on a rock, it'll stay there.

434
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:39,580
You hear my words, you don't do them, it's like building your house on sand, you might as well not have built it.

435
00:23:39,580 --> 00:23:40,240
Right?

436
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:41,740
To hear is to obey.

437
00:23:41,740 --> 00:23:42,940
You can't do one without the other.

438
00:23:42,940 --> 00:23:50,140
And now, there are times though, speaking in terms of your spouse, when despite knowing how much your spouse loves you,

439
00:23:50,140 --> 00:23:53,980
they don't behave the way you would expect them to or that you would like them to.

440
00:23:53,980 --> 00:24:00,020
And I'm sure we've all experienced that, not just with spouses, but siblings and employers and parents.

441
00:24:00,320 --> 00:24:04,880
And we say, where's the evidence of relationship here?

442
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:05,300
Right?

443
00:24:05,300 --> 00:24:10,100
Now, of course, if relationships are functioning the way they should, if you're functioning the way you should in a relationship,

444
00:24:10,100 --> 00:24:13,520
we look at ourselves, not at the other person, right?

445
00:24:13,520 --> 00:24:15,580
And we say, where's the evidence?

446
00:24:15,580 --> 00:24:19,600
Does my behavior square with the expected outcome of this relationship?

447
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:20,520
Am I being kind?

448
00:24:20,520 --> 00:24:21,280
Am I being faithful?

449
00:24:21,280 --> 00:24:22,140
Am I being reliable?

450
00:24:24,560 --> 00:24:32,880
And it's that need for self-reflection, for healthy relationship, that evaluation of how our behaviors look and what they mean about us.

451
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:39,520
That's what leads the New Testament authors to give us those lists of poor and preferred behaviors.

452
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:41,880
They're evaluating themselves.

453
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:42,980
They're evaluating their churches.

454
00:24:43,120 --> 00:24:55,200
And John makes this explicitly clear in Revelation 2, 4, and 5.

455
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:58,460
He says, but I have this against you that you've left your first love.

456
00:24:58,460 --> 00:24:59,920
Right?

457
00:25:00,280 --> 00:25:04,480
Therefore, remember from where you've fallen and repent and do the deeds you did at first.

458
00:25:04,480 --> 00:25:05,800
Okay?

459
00:25:05,800 --> 00:25:08,200
He correlates first love with first behavior.

460
00:25:08,200 --> 00:25:13,260
He's calling the church to be reconciled with their first love.

461
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:20,100
And the need for that reconciliation is indicated by their behaviors, which is manifestly clear in the parable of the prodigal son we read.

462
00:25:20,100 --> 00:25:20,380
Right?

463
00:25:20,380 --> 00:25:21,980
He needed to reconcile.

464
00:25:21,980 --> 00:25:23,040
You could tell from his behavior.

465
00:25:23,040 --> 00:25:29,060
And to mix a metaphor, in John 10, 27, he says, my sheep hear my voice and follow me.

466
00:25:29,060 --> 00:25:37,360
That's trust and devotion that a sheep have leads to expected behaviors, even in sheep.

467
00:25:37,360 --> 00:25:38,100
Right?

468
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:41,620
You don't have to be an adult human.

469
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:45,180
Everybody who has trust and devotion will act on that.

470
00:25:45,180 --> 00:25:51,860
They hear and obey and are reconciled once again to the shepherd that they're running away from.

471
00:25:51,860 --> 00:25:54,280
If you've ever kept sheep, it happens over and over.

472
00:25:54,280 --> 00:25:58,520
They get scared in a herd mentality and take off and you have to call them and they're like, oh, right, that makes sense.

473
00:25:58,520 --> 00:25:58,980
I like him.

474
00:25:58,980 --> 00:25:59,440
I trust him.

475
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:00,080
And they come back.

476
00:26:00,080 --> 00:26:00,620
Right?

477
00:26:00,620 --> 00:26:02,400
Over and over.

478
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:09,520
The need for reconciliation occurs to them when they hear the voice of the one they've come to know and trust.

479
00:26:10,200 --> 00:26:17,360
So to practically fulfill our vision of cultivating, proclaiming, and boldly obeying, we must come to know his voice through spending time with him.

480
00:26:17,360 --> 00:26:20,320
Because we, sheep-like, are easily distracted.

481
00:26:20,320 --> 00:26:22,100
